OL,3,GNEWSANew #632m contract to change
OL,4,Arubbish collection
OL,5,
OL,6,FChanges to how the rubbish for 190,000
OL,7,FSurrey households is collected are
OL,8,Fcoming after a new #632m waste contract
OL,9,Fwas agreed.
OL,11,FFor the past decade bins in Surrey
OL,12,FHeath, Woking, Runnymede and Elmbridge
OL,13,Fhave been collected under a joint waste
OL,14,Fpartnership, but that contract comes to
OL,15,Fan end this year after Amey decided it
OL,16,Fwas leaving the industry.
OL,18,FVeolia will take its place in a deal
OL,19,Fthat could last up to 21 years,
OL,20,Falthough it will first run for an
OL,21,Finitial seven-year period.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,328,320,200,140,0,100
